# ─── Cituna MCP server — configuration ────────────────────────────────
# The MCP server reads these from its process env. With Claude Desktop / Claude
# Code you normally set them in the MCP client config's "env" block (see README),
# not from a file. This file documents them and supports local `npm run dev`.

# Backend base URL. Defaults to the public backend if unset.
# Production (default): https://cituna.com
# Local backend dev:    http://localhost:3001
CITUNA_API_URL=https://cituna.com

# ── Auth: pick ONE option (checked in this priority order) ───────────────────

# Option 1 (RECOMMENDED) — a personal API key. In the app: Integrations → "Claude
# / MCP access" → Generate token, then paste the cituna_sk_… value here. Long-lived,
# revocable in the app, and not your password.
CITUNA_API_KEY=

# Option 2 — a session JWT. Log into the app, DevTools → Application → Cookies,
# copy the `cituna_token` value. Works but expires ~30 days after issue.
CITUNA_TOKEN=

# Option 3 — email/password. The server logs in and auto-refreshes on expiry.
CITUNA_EMAIL=
CITUNA_PASSWORD=
